# Lesson 2, new hand: open 1NT with 17, partner invites, accept.
title: Partner invites: accept with 17
id: L02-19
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4, 2.7
student: S
board: 19
dealer: S
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KT4    Q85    A9752  94
  E  Q752   A9732  4      Q65
  S  AJ6    K4     KQ83   KJ72
  W  983    JT6    JT6    AT83

auction:
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     key: 17 HCP and balanced: open 1NT.
     not 1D: Did you count 17? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT.
     not 1C: Did you count 17? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT.
     not *: Did you count 17? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 2NT    = 8-9 points, balanced: an invitation
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = A maximum: accept
     key: 17 is the top of your range. Accept the invitation.
     not Pass: Partner asks you to bid game with the top of your range. Is 17 the top?
     not *: Partner asks you to bid game with the top of your range. Is 17 the top?
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT invited game. With 17, the top of your range, your side
  has at least 25, so you accept. You are declarer, because you bid no-
  trump first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W HJ  N H5  E HA  S H4
  2   E H3  S HK  W H6  N H8
  3   S DK  W D6  N D2  E D4
      note: Run the diamonds, your longest suit together.
  4   S DQ  W DT  N D5  E C5
      note: Keep going.
  5   S D3  W DJ  N DA  E S2
      note: Over to dummy's ♦A.
  6   N D9  E C6  S D8  W C3
      note: Dummy's diamonds are all winners now.
  7   N D7  E S5  S C2  W C8
      note: The last diamond.
  8   N HQ  E H2  S C7  W HT
      note: Cash the ♥Q.
  9   N S4  E S7  S SA  W S3
      note: Now the spades: a spade to your ace.
  10  S S6  W S8  N SK  E SQ
      note: Back to dummy's king.
  11  N ST  E H7  S SJ  W S9
      note: Your ♠J is high now.
  12  S CK  W CA  N C4  E CQ
      note: Lead a club. West takes the ace.
  13  W CT  N C9  E H9  S CJ
      note: 11 tricks: 3NT made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  The plan: run the diamonds, then take your other winners.

  3NT made with two overtricks. Partner's five diamonds were worth five
  tricks once they joined your four.
